1
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,800
Nagasaki was rainy again today Nagasaki

2
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,960
I don't remember.

3
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:31,440
You caught that car thief who targeted only luxury cars last week,
didn't you?

4
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,940
That guy has something to do with Nagasaki?

5
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:37,360
He was wanted in Nagasaki.

6
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:40,560
Apparently he dismantled the cars
and sold the parts in Southeast Asia.

7
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:44,280
So they've asked for your
testimony on the arrest you made.

8
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:46,680
Is that all it was?

9
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,000
I thought you'd been put
on a wanted list, senpai.

10
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:52,460
Look, why would I ever
be put on a wanted list?

11
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,020
Well, Ryo-chan's reckless behavior is nationwide,
after all.

12
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:57,360
Sorry.

13
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:58,400
Ahahaha!

14
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:01,500
Well, let's keep that kind
of talk as just a joke.

15
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:01,900
Uchu!

16
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,100
What's that?

17
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,180
Isn't it obvious?

18
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:08,140
It's the airfare and hotel costs, of course.

19
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:10,160
Come on, don't play dumb.

20
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:12,720
Idiot, that's coming out of your own pocket!
Your own pocket!

21
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:13,640
Gah, no way!

22
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:15,840
That's what I'd like to say, but...

23
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,520
The station over there went
out of their way to send this.

24
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:22,640
It's the round-trip train fare between Tokyo and Nagasaki,
plus lodging.

25
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,960
Aren't we flying there?

26
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:27,380
The prefectural police don't
have much of a budget either.

27
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:30,140
Just be grateful they sent it at all.

28
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:34,920
By the way, Nagasaki is past Sendai, right?

29
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,960
Next to Iwate or something.

30
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:50,480
Hey, old man, one more drink.

31
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,460
Are you all right, Ryo-san?

32
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:54,700
What, my body?

33
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:57,040
Money? I don't have any money!

34
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:57,340
Yeah.

35
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:00,360
There is money here, I suppose.

36
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:03,940
But I can't use it.

37
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:05,580
Get it, old man?

38
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,520
No, never mind. Money's fine.

39
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,980
Hey, senpai. So you're here.

40
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:14,320
My wallet's here!

41
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:15,900
What are you talking about?

42
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:19,040
Ugh, don't worry about it.
Let's go to the next place.

43
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:21,060
You're covering this bill, got it?

44
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:22,500
Thanks for your business!

45
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,110
That's terrible, senpai.

46
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:31,160
I didn't even have a single sip,
and now I'm stuck paying for it all.

47
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,565
Hey, sorry, sorry.

48
00:02:32,615 --> 00:02:36,400
I drank a bit too much while waiting for you.
Here, drink up.

49
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:39,360
Of course I'll drink.
It's my money, isn't it?

50
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,180
Hahahaha!

51
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:45,880
Bepai. And I've got no
spare change left after that.

52
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:48,540
I still feel like I
haven't had enough to drink.

53
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,460
Me too, me too!

54
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,906
I drank it all.

55
00:02:54,956 --> 00:02:56,700
It all went on the tab.

56
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,380
Bepai, that's harsh.

57
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:03,002
Sorry about that. Don't cry. Just wait.

58
00:03:03,052 --> 00:03:06,420
If you look,
there's bound to be a coin or two.

59
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:13,495
Look at the main event. Here,

60
00:03:13,545 --> 00:03:15,480
I've got money, you know.

61
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,860
S-senpai!

62
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,890
Alright, now let's drink!

63
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:22,040
By the way, this money...

64
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,620
Senpai, let's hurry up and go drink.

65
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:53,920
What is it?

66
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:58,760
what are you doing standing there?

67
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,480
Chief.

68
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,100
We were discussing Japan's economy.

69
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,980
Chief,

70
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:08,400
since I'm taking paid leave anyway,
could I get three more days?

71
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,140
Why?

72
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:10,880
An opportunity like this
doesn't come along often,

73
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:14,700
so I thought I'd go to Nagasaki
early and broaden my horizons.

74
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:15,700
I see.

75
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,640
In that case, go ahead.

76
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:18,820
Well then, right away.

77
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,660
I'm leaving early today.

78
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:23,100
What's that supposed to mean?

79
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:25,340
Don't you have a lot
of preparations to make?

80
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:28,600
Fine, I'll just deduct
today's pay from your salary.

81
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,120
Senpai,
are you really planning to go by bicycle?

82
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:37,260
I have no money.
There's no other way, is there?

83
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:38,300
Are you serious?

84
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:41,400
It's a matter of pride for a man.
I have no choice but to do it.

85
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:42,660
I'm doing it.

86
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:46,280
Once I've made up my mind,
I won't back down.

87
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:47,760
Honestly.

88
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:58,100
It's already twelve o'clock?

89
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:00,780
Shouldn't we have reached
around Odawara by now?

90
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:02,080
Yotsuya.

91
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:06,340
I thought we'd come a long
way from Shinjuku, though.

92
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:09,120
We're still within Tokyo's 23 wards?
Damn it.

93
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:11,400
Tokyo is way too big.

94
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:16,820
Finally, Suginami Ward.

95
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,640
We're back in Shibuya Ward!

96
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:26,060
This is going to take
longer than I expected.

97
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:28,300
I need to rethink the plan.

98
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:31,360
Alright, let's go with this one.

99
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,380
Yes!

100
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:47,440
See? Even without money, as long as
you've got brains, you can make it work.

101
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:12,080
How much are the expressway
tolls for a bicycle?

102
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:19,420
Taking a bicycle on the expressway is more than just thrilling,
you know.

103
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:23,260
Crap, the tires are burning!

104
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,980
Super-high-speed electric massage!

105
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,980
What are you doing?

106
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:52,580
I'm showing the kids of the world what they should never do,
by example.

107
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:56,160
By the way, do you know the way to Nagasaki?

108
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:58,140
I don't know,
but why don't you just head for the sea?

109
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,860
If you follow the coast, you won't get lost.

110
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:02,100
Yeah, that makes sense. Thanks!

111
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:06,580
The sea! It's Enoshima!

112
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,700
I can't walk anymore, I'm about to collapse.

113
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:11,500
Collapse?

114
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,980
Right, I'm going to collapse!

115
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,080
Yes, this is Honda.

116
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:20,020
Senior, do you need something?

117
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:23,580
Hello? What's wrong, senior?

118
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:26,920
Hurry, it's Enoshima!

119
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,420
Enoshima? Has something happened?

120
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:31,320
It's no use.

121
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,720
Senior, hang in there!

122
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:35,380
Please, hurry!

123
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:38,560
Senior, senior!

124
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,760
Where? I'm on my way!

125
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:54,360
Honda!

126
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,820
Senpai!

127
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:00,320
Senpai!

128
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,940
Honda.

129
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,740
A little nap and I'm feeling refreshed.

130
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:11,000
I'm thirsty.

131
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,300
Think of it as a favor, and get me a juice.

132
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,400
Is that all?

133
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:17,480
You're really going to Nagasaki?

134
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:22,620
It's an honorable job, delivering me
to the Nagasaki Prefectural Police.

135
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:25,420
Just take me to Nagasaki,
that's all, what's the big deal?

136
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:27,100
That's not exactly a short distance, though.

137
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,620
Don't be shy about it.

138
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,820
Let's go!

139
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:32,220
Oh no.

140
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,520
Throwing away empty cans like
that is simply unacceptable.

141
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:42,640
You're a police officer, aren't you?

142
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,420
Sorry, sorry.

143
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:46,020
I fully meant to put it in the bin,

144
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:48,700
but making excuses isn't very manly.

145
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:51,060
People who don't follow etiquette
are the lowest of the low.

146
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:54,180
I said I meant to put it in the bin,
didn't I?

147
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:55,820
What's with that look on your face?

148
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:58,260
Anyway,
as long as I'm wearing a police uniform,

149
00:08:58,260 --> 00:08:59,860
you've got another thing coming
if you think I'll get scared.

150
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:01,860
This truck, Sister Haruyo,

151
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:02,880
don't you dare look down on her!

152
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:05,560
Come back when you've calmed down.

153
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:09,220
Stop your screeching!
You're not a crow at the garbage dump!

154
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:12,020
Look who's talking, with that face
like a gorilla that fell in a gutter!

155
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,540
What did you say!
A gorilla wearing a police uniform?

156
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:17,000
That's so ridiculous,
it'd make my belly button boil tea!

157
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:20,220
You're getting worked up! Then go ahead,
boil tea with your belly button!

158
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:23,820
I will!
Tea or coffee, just bring me a kettle!

159
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,480
A fight, a fight!

160
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,720
Hey, miss, want a hand?

161
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:33,140
In return, buy me a cup of tea.

162
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:34,360
Hehehehe.

163
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:36,880
Pick it up.

164
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:44,620
Pick up the cigarette you just threw away. Can't hear you.
Don't just brag with your mouth about the opposite sex, it's not a scandal, you know.

165
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:50,700
Shut up, don't act all high and mighty!
Let go of my hand.

166
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:58,700
What a feisty lady, I can't say the four-letter words!
I told you to let go of my hand!

167
00:09:59,320 --> 00:09:59,720
What?

168
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:08,620
Whoa! This guy!

169
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,020
Let go!

170
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:14,580
Now! Take him down!

171
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:17,180
Don't mess with me!

172
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:21,260
Hey, don't pull a cheap trick!
She's a woman!

173
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,540
You don't need to butt in!

174
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:24,940
I see.

175
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:32,160
Not bad at all.

176
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:35,180
Isn't there a trash can
to throw these away in?

177
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:44,420
Picking up litter is police work, is it? Well,
leave it to you. Those cars are in the way of traffic.

178
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:48,640
Pull over to the side!
Yes, yes, Gorilla Policeman.

179
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:53,880
Empty cans go in the trash.
I'm a skilled gorilla cop, you know.

180
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:04,900
I'm totally overwhelmed

181
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:07,440
A female truck driver

182
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:12,340
It's cold, isn't it.

183
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:17,020
I came all the way to Hakone,
and there are no hot springs?

184
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:19,720
Then I shouldn't have
gone drinking yesterday.

185
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,500
Don't say that.

186
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:23,460
The cold really gets to you, doesn't it.

187
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:30,700
No matter how far we go,
it's nothing but mountains.

188
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:32,220
I'm in Hakone, after all.

189
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:34,160
You're not getting lost, are you?

190
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:36,020
We're heading west.

191
00:11:36,020 --> 00:11:38,520
Mount Fuji is visible on our right,
after all.

192
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:42,460
You'd better learn to read a map at least.

193
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:44,680
Shut up, mind your own business.

194
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:47,920
The sea!

195
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:01,500
We're out of gas.

196
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:04,240
What should we do, senpai?

197
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:07,440
Can't we do something?
Even just for gasoline?

198
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:10,100
Let's ask the bus to give us some gasoline.

199
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:12,860
Buses don't run on gasoline, you know.

200
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:14,360
It's a joke, just a joke.

201
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:17,380
Are you so hungry you
can't even take a joke?

202
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:20,580
Speaking of Hamanaka, it's eel, isn't it?

203
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:22,240
Eel

204
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:26,160
I want to eat eel, eel, eel!

205
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,580
Needs must, I suppose.

206
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,720
What's wrong with your stomach?

207
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:33,280
Stomach?

208
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:34,980
Yes, my stomach!

209
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:36,360
My stomach...

210
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,200
Senpai!

211
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,260
I'm so hungry my belly
button has moved to my back!

212
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,020
Senpai!

213
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:44,600
Ow ow!

214
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:45,420
This is bad.

215
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:48,360
Honda, bring me a lot of water.

216
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:50,340
Yes.

217
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:57,800
Senpai, I brought you water.

218
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,620
Thanks.

219
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:02,040
Senpai, are you okay?

220
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,760
My stomach's gone all the
way around and back to normal.

221
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:06,400
Let's go eat some eel.

222
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:07,860
Oh, yes.

223
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:13,100
Wow, what a feast!

224
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:14,880
Thank you for the meal.

225
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:17,180
So good!

226
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:21,000
Still, you're a sneaky one, Senpai.

227
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,920
You had money, didn't you?

228
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,240
Well, yeah.

229
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:26,140
Today's journey ends here.

230
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,720
Come on, eat and drink!

231
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:32,900
I ate and ate.

232
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:34,100
Drank and drank.

233
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:36,020
Next, the bath! The hot spring!

234
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:37,540
An outdoor bath!

235
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,360
I'm first!

236
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:42,720
Yaaah!

237
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:45,560
Ow

238
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:46,500
Senpai?

239
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:49,140
Y-you're totally exposed!

240
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,200
You molester, you pervert!

241
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,600
Littering, and now peeping?

242
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,680
Unpopular guys are so shameless.

243
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:00,380
You female truck-driving bastard!

244
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:01,740
What's with that face?

245
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:05,060
You did something wrong and
don't have a shred of remorse?

246
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:08,580
Even a monkey can feel remorse,
you gorilla-man!

247
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:12,480
Hey, take a look at this.

248
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,660
And then this one is...

249
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:17,940
Look, the one who made the mistake is you.

250
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:19,400
I messed up.

251
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,860
Mistakes like this happen all the time,
don't they?

252
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,580
Being short-tempered is a problem too.

253
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:26,140
That's what they call a hothead.

254
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:31,420
Make sure you check whether you've got one or not,
alright?

255
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,680
Whoa, too close!

256
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,000
Oh no, I blew it!

257
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,900
Please be careful.

258
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:47,620
What do you want me to do?
It's artificial, artificial!

259
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,440
Well then.

260
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,620
Take care.

261
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:58,020
She was a pretty nice person, wasn't she.

262
00:14:58,020 --> 00:14:59,600
Alright, let's go.

263
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:03,120
Don't dawdle!
Nagasaki is still a long way off.

264
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:05,900
By the way, what about my bike?

265
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:10,580
Senpai, don't tell me the
hotel money and everything...

266
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:14,200
Don't worry. Just pay the money
back before it gets forfeited.

267
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:18,480
So you met up with them using the
money from pawning my bike at Nanaya?

268
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:21,640
That's terrible, pawning my bike at Nanaya!

269
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:25,520
You were having fun too, weren't you!

270
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:27,440
But my bike...

271
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,560
So how are we supposed
to get to Nagasaki now?

272
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:31,700
Well, obviously...

273
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:40,440
Senpai, it won't stop at all!

274
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,700
Damn it, even in uniform,
Katsushika is hopeless after all?

275
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:52,280
We just walked around the port
and the sun's already gone down.

276
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:58,740
I'm getting hungry.
Senpai, where are we staying tonight?

277
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:03,700
Do we still have any money left?
Hey, Senpai, come on!

278
00:16:04,390 --> 00:16:08,880
Ugh, you're so annoying! Just leave everything to me,
leave it all to me!

279
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:13,860
It's this way, we're heading over there.

280
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,000
Here, here!

281
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:21,540
I just remembered.

282
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:23,260
This is my relative's house.

283
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:25,160
Our senior relative's

284
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:28,460
father's cousin's third son's wife's

285
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:29,900
cousin Hatoko's house.

286
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:32,600
Uncle, good evening!

287
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,540
Uncle, are you home?

288
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:36,240
Yes, who's there?

289
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:38,060
Uncle, long time no see!

290
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:39,060
You're...

291
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:40,760
Glad to see you're doing well.

292
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:42,220
How many years has it been?

293
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:53,360
Nah, hey Honda, come on in! Good evening! This is Honda, my friend.
He really wanted to meet Uncle, so he tagged along. Grandma!

294
00:16:53,360 --> 00:17:02,540
Grandma's here, here! That's great. Standing out here talking isn't right, Grandma.
We came to visit from Tokyo. Good evening!

295
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:12,080
Well, the house hasn't changed at all. It's just like before.
Good, good. So you came all the way from Tokyo?

296
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:16,280
Your youngest brother,
didn't he move to Tokyo?

297
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:18,840
Then, you're my nephew Hiroshi?

298
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,060
Yes, Hiroshi. That's the one.

299
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:22,660
Who's Hiroshi?

300
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:25,760
Good, good, you remembered me.

301
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,279
I see, so you're Hiroshi-kun.

302
00:17:27,329 --> 00:17:30,040
You've changed so much
I didn't recognize you.

303
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:31,508
Right? Right?

304
00:17:31,558 --> 00:17:34,320
Everyone says that.
"You've changed, you've changed."

305
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:38,180
How's your cousin Heisuke doing?
Is he well? Well, well.

306
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:39,980
Heisuke passed away, you know.

307
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:42,520
Yes, yes,
he went and passed away healthy as can be.

308
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,320
I seem to be hungry again.

309
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:50,360
Honda's so hungry he's collapsed.

310
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:53,600
Well, well, let's have dinner, dear.

311
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:55,600
Yes, for Hiroshi-kun.

312
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:58,540
I know, it's been a long time, hasn't it?

313
00:17:58,540 --> 00:18:01,260
Sorry, it seems we've been making demands.

314
00:18:01,260 --> 00:18:02,780
Not at all.

315
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:07,040
No, Auntie is so thoughtful and kind.

316
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:08,680
Uncle, you're a happy man.

317
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:10,820
Not really.

318
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:16,840
You really are an interesting one,
Hiroshi-kun.

319
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:19,000
We still have plenty
of things to talk about.

320
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,260
Shall we drink through the night tonight?

321
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,320
Come on, Honda-kun, drink some more.

322
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:27,660
Thank you very much.

323
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:34,140
This door's really hard to open

324
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:35,780
Let me take a look.

325
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:39,700
It'd be better to shave it down a bit.

326
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:40,940
Is there really such a thing?

327
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:42,980
You don't have to do that.

328
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,220
You're a guest, after all.

329
00:18:44,220 --> 00:18:45,780
Don't worry about it, don't worry about it.

330
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:47,140
I'm great at this kind of thing.

331
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:48,080
Leave it to me.

332
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,380
That should do it, I guess.

333
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:53,720
You're really good at this, aren't you.

334
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,460
Didn't I tell you? I'm very good at this.

335
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:57,280
Is there anything else?

336
00:18:57,280 --> 00:18:58,120
Is that so?

337
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:58,620
But...

338
00:18:58,620 --> 00:19:00,080
No, no, it's fine, really.

339
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:02,380
Roof, plumbing, anything's fine.

340
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:04,040
Here you go, Uncle.

341
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:04,840
Thank you very much.

342
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:06,900
So, all the way to Kyushu, then.

343
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:09,040
Yes, I have some business to attend to.

344
00:19:10,460 --> 00:19:12,040
Things are wobbly all
over the place, though.

345
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,440
They'll be fine if they're maintained.

346
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:16,320
I'll come back,
and I'll do it all again then.

347
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,840
You sure can sleep

348
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:27,040
They're such nice people,
and I feel bad for deceiving them.

349
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:34,440
Well then, take care on your way.

350
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:36,640
Here, this is a bento for you.

351
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:38,100
This is much appreciated.

352
00:19:38,770 --> 00:19:40,980
Kyushu is still a long way off, you know.

353
00:19:41,590 --> 00:19:43,440
No, thanks for everything.

354
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,380
Well, see you.

355
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:48,540
Stop by again on your way back, Hiroshi.

356
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:49,360
Yeah.

357
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:57,220
Senpai, please go on ahead.

358
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,440
What's wrong? Did you forget something?

359
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:08,240
Well, actually, about that Hiroshi-kun...

360
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:13,720
We're all connected by fate, you know.

361
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,780
Thanks to you,
I had a great time last night.

362
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:16,480
Yes.

363
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,980
Well then...

364
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:21,080
Now that I think about it,
Hiroshi is still just a middle schooler.

365
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,580
Thank you for everything.

366
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,160
Senpai.

367
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,900
Nice morning, isn't it, senpai.

368
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:40,480
Come on, cheer up and let's walk all the way to Nagasaki!
Let's go!

369
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,440
Senpai, I can't walk anymore.

370
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:49,400
Stop whining every step of the way!
Where did your energy from before go?

371
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:52,800
But my legs are all swollen,
I can't take a single step!

372
00:20:53,580 --> 00:20:55,920
If you think you can walk,
you can walk anywhere.

373
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:00,440
You're walking to Nagasaki, remember?
Come on!

374
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:07,420
I'm just unlucky. Nagasaki is impossible!
Just come on already.

375
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:12,600
You said we'd go together!
No way, I don't want to, I really don't!

376
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:23,260
What are you doing standing over there?

377
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:37,000
Pawning the bike and splurging like that,

378
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,200
you really are an outrageous guy.

379
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:41,020
But we really got lucky.

380
00:21:41,560 --> 00:21:44,160
Being on our way to Nagasaki by pure luck,

381
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:46,720
it feels like a huge stroke of luck.

382
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:48,760
Walking all the way to Nagasaki,

383
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:51,480
that's beyond reckless.
Only an idiot would do that.

384
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:52,660
What do you mean, idiot?

385
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:53,840
If you put your mind to it, you can do it.

386
00:21:54,420 --> 00:21:56,200
Do you have any idea how
many days that will take?

387
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,340
When I say I'll do something, I do it.

388
00:21:58,340 --> 00:22:00,000
There's no way you can do that.

389
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,260
I can! I'll start right now.

390
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:07,140
Senpai, what are you doing? Please stop!

391
00:22:07,140 --> 00:22:09,340
Shut up and talk!

392
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:11,960
Don't stop me, you idiot!

393
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:16,760
What the heck is this?

394
00:22:20,780 --> 00:22:22,140
It's just a cat.

395
00:22:22,140 --> 00:22:25,340
Hey, don't lick me so much.

396
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:29,060
Looks like it likes you, senpai.

397
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:33,400
What's its name? Tamasaburo, hey, stop it!

398
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:37,780
In human terms,
you've got the face of a vicious criminal!

399
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:44,960
But it looks just like you, senpai.
Don't joke! I don't look like that!

400
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:50,380
It's a face that females like more than males.
Tamasaburo's a female, you know.

401
00:22:50,380 --> 00:22:53,740
What? Stop it already!

402
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:57,280
Hey, this thing won't get off me at all!

403
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:59,200
At this rate, I can't get down at all.

404
00:22:59,760 --> 00:23:02,200
Fine, I'll let you ride
all the way to Nagasaki.

405
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:04,940
Fine, I'll let you ride.

406
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:07,420
Hey, don't lick my nostrils!

407
00:23:41,540 --> 00:23:44,620
Hey, Goran, don't sleep on my lap.
You're heavy.

408
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:46,900
Goran, wake up, Tamasaburo.

409
00:23:47,700 --> 00:23:49,920
Just one more stretch and
we'll be in Nagasaki, right?

410
00:23:53,380 --> 00:23:57,140
What's wrong?
You've been silent this whole time.

411
00:24:01,300 --> 00:24:02,100
Moved?

412
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:05,540
Yeah, four years ago.

413
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:09,600
Get out!

414
00:24:11,980 --> 00:24:15,380
You're no longer my child,
and I'm no longer your parent.

415
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:17,360
From today,
you're a complete stranger to me.

416
00:24:17,980 --> 00:24:19,180
Fine, I'm leaving.

417
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:23,240
Who'd want to stay with a stubborn,
unreasonable old fool like you?

418
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:27,780
With a personality like that,
even men run away from you

419
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:29,240
It's not like I got dumped.

420
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:33,480
He's a man, yet he dragged his feet and wouldn't cut it off,
so I was the one who dumped him.

421
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:37,260
Then you shouldn't have brushed off the marriage match I recommended,
should you?

422
00:24:37,260 --> 00:24:39,660
I don't like it, and that's that.

423
00:24:41,540 --> 00:24:45,260
Dad, Haruyo,
let's both calm down and talk this through.

424
00:24:45,260 --> 00:24:47,660
Stop your nagging!
I've already made up my mind.

425
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:51,300
Once I've decided, even if the sun
rises in the west, I won't change.

426
00:24:51,300 --> 00:24:53,320
Well, I'm not so easy either!

427
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:54,860
Haruyo.

428
00:24:54,860 --> 00:24:56,560
Don't you dare freak out.

429
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:09,460
That was that.

430
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:14,080
So you turned down the marriage
prospect your father favored?

431
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:16,240
Well, that's just like you.

432
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:22,120
Dad's the type who can't be satisfied
unless everything goes his way.

433
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:26,240
So what made you suddenly decide to go home?

434
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:28,940
We got word that he collapsed.

435
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:31,960
And since I had work nearby,

436
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:34,460
I figured I'd stop by while I was at it.

437
00:25:34,460 --> 00:25:35,720
Four years.

438
00:25:36,780 --> 00:25:38,180
I worked hard,

439
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:40,880
and finally bought this truck.

440
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:46,660
You really went through a lot, didn't you?

441
00:25:46,660 --> 00:25:47,820
Yeah, well.

442
00:25:48,320 --> 00:25:50,000
Alright, we're here at Glover Garden!

443
00:25:58,200 --> 00:26:03,680
Sorry, Tamasaburo. I'll be right back,
so just wait quietly in here.

444
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:11,660
So how is your father doing?

445
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:16,600
Doesn't seem so good.
He says it's hard even to get up.

446
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,800
I'm afraid he'll end up bedridden like this.

447
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:22,780
Mom's worried about it.

448
00:26:25,860 --> 00:26:27,460
Is there a festival today?

449
00:26:28,780 --> 00:26:30,300
Yeah, the Hansen Festival.

450
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:40,220
Dad's on a fishing boat too,
even though he used to be a captain.

451
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:42,980
His drinking too much
finally caught up with him.

452
00:26:44,780 --> 00:26:48,180
Apparently he can't even go see the
festival and is just moping around.

453
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:52,100
He might get better, you know.

454
00:26:52,740 --> 00:26:53,680
I know.

455
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:57,040
Then stop dawdling around here.

456
00:26:57,580 --> 00:27:00,620
I know already.
Your meddling is none of your business.

457
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:03,540
Come on, let's go.

458
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,780
What are you doing?

459
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:09,100
Senpai, where do you mean to go?

460
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:11,480
To that father of yours, obviously.

461
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:13,320
Wait a minute.

462
00:27:13,320 --> 00:27:15,340
You haven't decided to go yet, have you?

463
00:27:16,180 --> 00:27:17,560
I said wait a minute!

464
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:18,780
You idiot.

465
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:25,920
came back to Nagasaki, didn't you? Or do you mean after
your father has already become a Buddha, too late to see him?

466
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:32,720
would be better? I'm just like your father,
I have to have things my way.

467
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:37,660
or I won't be satisfied. If you absolutely refuse,
I'll tie you up with rope

468
00:27:37,660 --> 00:27:40,600
and take you anyway, Ryo-san.

469
00:27:41,900 --> 00:27:43,340
What...

470
00:27:50,180 --> 00:27:51,200
My truck!

471
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:52,540
It's a truck thief!

472
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:53,400
Wait!

473
00:27:58,480 --> 00:27:59,440
Tamasaburo!

474
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:03,040
S-s-senpai!

475
00:28:03,040 --> 00:28:05,640
Damn it, I won't let him get away with it!

476
00:28:10,580 --> 00:28:11,680
Excuse me, sorry.

477
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:15,360
We're with the police,
and we're tracking that truck.

478
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,300
Please lend me that bike.

479
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:18,240
Yes.

480
00:28:23,880 --> 00:28:24,920
You're not getting away!

481
00:28:25,740 --> 00:28:26,760
Hurry up and get on!

482
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:29,000
Y-yes!

483
00:28:30,140 --> 00:28:31,260
Let's go!

484
00:28:36,560 --> 00:28:38,745
Right,

485
00:28:38,795 --> 00:28:42,520
Damn it!

486
00:28:49,140 --> 00:28:51,080
Lord! Are you all right?

487
00:28:51,760 --> 00:28:53,040
Help me!

488
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:58,940
Tamasaburo!

489
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:13,200
Is that okay?

490
00:29:14,380 --> 00:29:17,080
Hey, police! Stop the truck!

491
00:29:26,580 --> 00:29:27,660
Samura!

492
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:27,720
Samura!

493
00:29:35,820 --> 00:29:37,260
Don't take me for a fool like this!

494
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:41,460
You bastard!

495
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,280
Tamasaburoooo!

496
00:29:57,820 --> 00:29:59,340
Where is he? Where is he?

497
00:30:04,480 --> 00:30:05,760
Tamasaburo!

498
00:30:09,260 --> 00:30:10,440
Haruyo-san

499
00:30:11,040 --> 00:30:12,200
Take care of this guy for me.

500
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:16,000
Senpai

501
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:26,000
Tamasaburou!

502
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:29,880
I'm sorry,
I put you through something scary, didn't I?

503
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:30,600
Good thing it wasn't impossible.

504
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:44,200
S-senpai

505
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:53,900
That was a close call.

506
00:30:53,900 --> 00:30:55,520
Thank goodness.

507
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:57,280
Ryo-san

508
00:30:59,120 --> 00:30:59,860
Thank you.

509
00:31:08,480 --> 00:31:10,700
Don't mention it.

510
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:23,700
Dad, I'm just going out to do some shopping.

511
00:31:29,080 --> 00:31:31,160
Tamasaburo.

512
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:32,760
Excuse me.

513
00:31:33,580 --> 00:31:34,780
Hello.

514
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:37,520
Something...

515
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:42,200
Come on, what are you doing? Hurry up!

516
00:31:43,220 --> 00:31:44,880
Haruyo.

517
00:31:47,320 --> 00:31:48,960
Dad, Dad!

518
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:51,620
Haruyo's back! Haruyo's come home!

519
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:52,360
What?

520
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:54,520
She's at the entrance right now.

521
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:56,320
Wait!

522
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:59,240
He's moved, I tell you.

523
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:01,280
I'm not letting him straddle the globe!

524
00:32:01,280 --> 00:32:01,920
No way.

525
00:32:03,660 --> 00:32:04,380
Dad

526
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:06,680
I don't know you.

527
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:09,000
I'm not feeling well.

528
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:10,260
Just go home.

529
00:32:10,260 --> 00:32:14,020
I didn't come back because I wanted to borrow anything,
you know.

530
00:32:14,020 --> 00:32:16,460
I just happened to be passing by.

531
00:32:16,460 --> 00:32:17,940
So I just stopped in for a moment.

532
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:19,540
I'm going.

533
00:32:19,540 --> 00:32:20,620
Wait.

534
00:32:22,340 --> 00:32:23,680
Who the hell are you?

535
00:32:24,940 --> 00:32:27,320
Well, I've heard everything.

536
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:28,320
Ryo-san,

537
00:32:29,060 --> 00:32:30,540
So you've gone and married him, have you?

538
00:32:30,540 --> 00:32:32,660
It's none of your business, you know.

539
00:32:32,660 --> 00:32:35,160
But it became my business, didn't it?

540
00:32:35,160 --> 00:32:35,920
This is

541
00:32:35,920 --> 00:32:39,000
I'm engaged to your daughter.

542
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:40,320
What did you say?

543
00:32:40,320 --> 00:32:41,620
Ryo-san,

544
00:32:41,620 --> 00:32:43,460
Say that again.

545
00:32:44,020 --> 00:32:46,840
Yes, so I'm

546
00:32:47,540 --> 00:32:56,260
It's true, we're madly in love!
Is it really? Absolutely true, Haruyo!

547
00:32:56,680 --> 00:33:06,140
Don't you dare touch my daughter so familiarly! Weren't you a complete stranger?
If you disowned her, you're neither her father nor her child.

548
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:11,080
If you're going to object,
lift your daughter's disownment first.

549
00:33:12,500 --> 00:33:14,060
All you do is spout sophistry.

550
00:33:15,140 --> 00:33:18,280
Well then,
we'll live happily just the two of us.

551
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:21,120
Having a stubborn old father
like you just gets in the way.

552
00:33:21,560 --> 00:33:23,860
No way, I won't allow it!

553
00:33:24,380 --> 00:33:25,860
No matter what you say,

554
00:33:25,860 --> 00:33:28,980
we can marry by our own choice, you know.

555
00:33:28,980 --> 00:33:30,880
No, no, no!

556
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:32,920
She's my daughter, dammit!

557
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:34,720
It's too late now.

558
00:33:36,940 --> 00:33:37,800
Wait a minute!

559
00:33:40,380 --> 00:33:44,780
I won't give my daughter
to a frivolous man like you.

560
00:33:44,780 --> 00:33:47,240
Then who would be acceptable?

561
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:53,500
So if a man meets your approval,
you don't care if my daughter objects?

562
00:33:53,500 --> 00:33:56,600
I'm only thinking of
my daughter's happiness.

563
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:58,220
Are you touched?

564
00:34:00,220 --> 00:34:05,880
If you truly cared about your daughter's happiness, you'd let her do as she wishes.
That's what a parent does.

565
00:34:06,140 --> 00:34:10,380
You're just clinging to your
own pride and stubbornness.

566
00:34:10,380 --> 00:34:12,880
How could a man like you
understand a parent's feelings?

567
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:14,120
You stubborn old geezer!

568
00:34:14,120 --> 00:34:17,980
You centipede-browed, bushy-eyebrowed freak!

569
00:34:17,980 --> 00:34:19,880
You fossil from another era!

570
00:34:19,880 --> 00:34:22,440
You caveman gorilla-bear!

571
00:34:23,020 --> 00:34:25,880
You thick-headed blockhead,
you pumpkin-brained dolt!

572
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:30,580
Father.

573
00:34:36,140 --> 00:34:38,640
Dad, you can stand up!

574
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:40,160
Really?

575
00:34:42,760 --> 00:34:43,640
Tamazakura

576
00:34:45,140 --> 00:34:47,580
Well, well, you came back.

577
00:34:50,040 --> 00:34:51,320
Dad.

578
00:34:54,820 --> 00:34:56,060
I was so lonely.

579
00:34:56,060 --> 00:34:57,620
Without you here,

580
00:34:58,140 --> 00:34:59,980
you were my only reason to live.

581
00:35:01,380 --> 00:35:03,480
Don't go anywhere again.

582
00:35:04,040 --> 00:35:04,820
Dad.

583
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:07,320
Well, that's good then.

584
00:35:09,660 --> 00:35:10,800
Wait, Ryo-san.

585
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:12,640
Thank you.

586
00:35:14,220 --> 00:35:15,480
Thank you, Ryo-san.

587
00:35:16,540 --> 00:35:17,900
Hey, cut that out.

588
00:35:17,900 --> 00:35:19,180
The act's over.

589
00:35:19,180 --> 00:35:20,040
Acting.

590
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:22,360
So, rest assured.

591
00:35:23,060 --> 00:35:24,800
I thought as much.

592
00:35:25,380 --> 00:35:27,260
Haruyo's picky about looks, isn't she?

593
00:35:32,420 --> 00:35:36,160
But if she found a pretty boy like him,
she might be willing to marry.

594
00:35:38,700 --> 00:35:40,040
Don't joke around.

595
00:35:57,260 --> 00:35:57,540
Mm.

596
00:35:59,320 --> 00:36:04,520
Good for you, Dad! You finally got to
ride the boat you've been dying to ride!

597
00:36:05,540 --> 00:36:07,340
All thanks to Haruyo.

598
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:15,500
I'm not going back to Tokyo.
I'm getting my boat license.

599
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:19,120
I'm going to live here. I see.

600
00:36:19,120 --> 00:36:20,400
Aaaah.

601
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:29,100
Aaaah, another big catch today.

602
00:36:31,260 --> 00:36:32,400
Welcome back!

603
00:36:32,760 --> 00:36:33,920
Daddy!

604
00:36:36,960 --> 00:36:39,500
Today we're having sukiyaki,
Daddy's favorite!

605
00:36:39,700 --> 00:36:40,560
I see!

606
00:36:43,620 --> 00:36:46,160
Being a man of the sea
isn't so bad after all.

607
00:36:54,220 --> 00:36:57,620
Do you think it'd be all right
to call in someone like those two?

608
00:36:59,640 --> 00:37:00,580
Look...

609
00:37:03,560 --> 00:37:06,040
Uh what?

610
00:37:09,860 --> 00:37:12,360
W-why is there a giant dolphin here?

611
00:37:12,940 --> 00:37:14,060
It's a dolphin.

612
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:16,460
What's wrong?

613
00:37:16,540 --> 00:37:18,120
No, it's nothing.

614
00:37:18,120 --> 00:37:19,840
Let's just pretend we didn't see that.

615
00:37:23,500 --> 00:37:27,480
Ryo-san, you were about to say something earlier.
What is it?

616
00:37:28,780 --> 00:37:30,460
Well look.

617
00:37:32,940 --> 00:37:33,320
What?

618
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:39,140
Wow.

619
00:37:43,040 --> 00:37:45,280
Why is Swimsuit Deka here?

620
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:47,040
What's wrong?

621
00:37:47,600 --> 00:37:50,780
Nothing. Let's pretend we didn't see that.

622
00:37:53,960 --> 00:37:55,260
Listen...

623
00:37:55,260 --> 00:37:55,540
What?

624
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:04,140
Why is Moonlight Deka here?

625
00:38:04,140 --> 00:38:05,780
What's wrong?

626
00:38:05,780 --> 00:38:08,220
Nope, let's pretend we didn't see that.

627
00:38:09,420 --> 00:38:11,420
Do you have something to say?

628
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:13,247
Well

629
00:38:13,297 --> 00:38:16,060
I've been thinking it's about time,
that I...

630
00:38:17,580 --> 00:38:18,500
Tamasaburo

631
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:28,340
Ken

632
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:30,800
Haruyo

633
00:38:31,580 --> 00:38:32,060
What?

634
00:38:34,620 --> 00:38:35,980
When did she come back?

635
00:38:37,040 --> 00:38:37,520
Today.

636
00:38:38,180 --> 00:38:38,660
I

637
00:38:39,300 --> 00:38:40,040
That time,

638
00:38:40,040 --> 00:38:41,480
right after coming back from the voyage,

639
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:42,800
I went straight over

640
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:44,400
to Haruyo's place,

641
00:38:45,520 --> 00:38:47,700
but Haruyo was already gone.

642
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:48,840
Ken

643
00:38:52,840 --> 00:38:54,240
You're boarding a foreign ship?

644
00:38:54,900 --> 00:38:56,680
When will you come back?

645
00:38:57,740 --> 00:39:00,020
I can't be the one to say it.

646
00:39:02,940 --> 00:39:03,500
Haruyo...

647
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:06,980
You idiot, you idiot.

648
00:39:07,460 --> 00:39:09,520
Why didn't you ask me to wait for you?

649
00:39:12,140 --> 00:39:13,440
I was the fool.

650
00:39:14,400 --> 00:39:16,520
I've regretted it ever since.

651
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:17,200
Ken.

652
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:23,980
If you're willing...

653
00:39:26,300 --> 00:39:28,560
Will you stay by my side forever?

654
00:39:36,700 --> 00:39:38,420
So it's all right, Haruyo?

655
00:39:45,420 --> 00:39:47,120
There's someone I want to introduce you to.

656
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:48,680
Ryo... that...

657
00:40:05,340 --> 00:40:06,220
In the end,

658
00:40:06,220 --> 00:40:08,960
I didn't have a part to play after all.

659
00:40:10,340 --> 00:40:12,780
The lovers kept missing each other,

660
00:40:12,780 --> 00:40:15,480
and four years have passed just like that.

661
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:16,340
Hey,

662
00:40:16,340 --> 00:40:17,220
Tamasaburo!

663
00:40:18,680 --> 00:40:19,200
He's gone.

664
00:40:21,380 --> 00:40:22,500
What's he doing?

665
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:24,400
Is it a rat?

666
00:40:26,180 --> 00:40:27,340
Hey, Tamasaburo.

667
00:40:27,340 --> 00:40:28,380
Come back.

668
00:40:31,080 --> 00:40:32,820
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for your patience.

669
00:40:33,300 --> 00:40:34,420
The annual

670
00:40:34,420 --> 00:40:35,880
fireworks festival is about to begin.

671
00:40:35,880 --> 00:40:37,140
Please enjoy yourselves.

672
00:40:37,140 --> 00:40:39,880
Where did Senpai go?

673
00:40:40,620 --> 00:40:41,420
Honda-san.

674
00:40:41,420 --> 00:40:44,680
Haruyo-san, do you know where Senpai is?

675
00:40:45,120 --> 00:40:47,020
We were looking for her too.

676
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:53,060
Ken Ankura-san, hello. We're

677
00:40:53,060 --> 00:41:01,060
Getting married?!
So that's why Senpai disappeared...

678
00:41:02,220 --> 00:41:03,340
Hey! Tamasaburo!

679
00:41:04,340 --> 00:41:04,940
Yah!

680
00:41:05,100 --> 00:41:07,060
Got it! Heave-ho!

681
00:41:07,540 --> 00:41:08,140
Whoa!

682
00:41:08,460 --> 00:41:09,460
What the heck is this!

683
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:14,080
Hey, you! Tamasaburo!

684
00:41:14,260 --> 00:41:16,640
I said wait! Wait... Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

685
00:41:17,120 --> 00:41:19,180
Alright! The launch is starting!

686
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:20,600
Fight!

687
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:21,500
Hup!

688
00:41:27,020 --> 00:41:29,060
Wow! Strong!

689
00:41:42,720 --> 00:41:47,180
I'm sure the senior officer is
watching these fireworks somewhere too.

690
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,120
Whoa!

691
00:41:51,960 --> 00:41:54,420
No way! That can't be!

692
00:41:58,460 --> 00:42:00,760
I see. Understood.

693
00:42:03,560 --> 00:42:05,120
Was that from the Nagasaki
Prefectural Police?

694
00:42:05,740 --> 00:42:10,700
Apparently Ryotsu never even showed his face
at the prefectural police and has gone missing.

695
00:42:10,700 --> 00:42:14,520
He got to Nagasaki,
so what on earth happened to him?

696
00:42:15,480 --> 00:42:18,180
He must be out somewhere,
goofing off without a care.

697
00:42:18,180 --> 00:42:20,340
When he gets back,
we'll give him a good scolding.

698
00:42:23,460 --> 00:42:26,060
Hello, this is Kameari Kōen-mae police box.

699
00:42:26,060 --> 00:42:28,640
Ryotsu?

700
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:31,740
Idiot! Where are you right now?

701
00:42:32,060 --> 00:42:34,140
I'm in Hakodate right now.

702
00:42:34,620 --> 00:42:39,020
Hakodate? How did you end up there when
you were supposed to be in Nagasaki?

703
00:42:39,020 --> 00:42:41,740
Well, in Nagasaki I got
blasted up with the fireworks,

704
00:42:41,740 --> 00:42:45,260
then I got caught on an airplane,
and the place I came down was Hakodate.

705
00:42:45,260 --> 00:42:47,900
What nonsense are you babbling about?

706
00:42:47,900 --> 00:42:50,760
Anyway, Chief, please send me
money for the travel expenses.

707
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:53,980
Ugh, I don't want to know
someone like you anymore.

708
00:42:53,980 --> 00:42:57,020
Just become a crab in Hokkaido already!

709
00:42:57,540 --> 00:42:59,180
No, Chief! Chief!

710
00:42:59,180 --> 00:43:06,080
Noooo! Don't say that!
How am I supposed to get back from here?!

711
00:43:30,460 --> 00:43:37,920
Dawdling around the corner,
the moon runs off and the race begins

712
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:45,520
Right now isn't everything,
so don't get too worked up.

713
00:43:45,520 --> 00:43:53,440
A little lying, a little cheating,
but sometimes you're helping someone.

714
00:43:53,440 --> 00:43:57,520
Baby, do you know me?
Heading toward tomorrow

715
00:43:57,520 --> 00:43:59,840
Nice spirit

716
00:44:00,900 --> 00:44:04,880
Don't give up, I'll do what needs doing.

717
00:44:04,880 --> 00:44:07,240
Cute spirit

718
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:10,700
What's hard to understand is

719
00:44:11,680 --> 00:44:14,300
wanting to appear that way

720
00:44:14,820 --> 00:44:20,380
Better than being all show, right?

721
00:44:22,020 --> 00:44:27,040
na na na na na na na na na na na na

